MyGo patch 0022 (VoxtNew): Window.IsOnActiveSpace.

VoxtNew's Rewrite card is an ordinary window that takes the front when
the user acts on it (cardFront): VoxtNew is activated with the card as
its key window. On another app's full-screen Space, macOS shows no
ordinary window of a regular app (one with a Dock icon), even one that
is visible on all workspaces and an auxiliary of full-screen Spaces; and
activating the app from there switches to a desktop with its windows,
taking the user out of their full-screen app.

IsOnActiveSpace reports NSWindow.isOnActiveSpace, which for a hidden
window tells whether ordering it in would put it on the active Space: an
app can tell before showing a window that it cannot show there, and use
a panel (WindowOptions.Panel), which shows over full-screen apps and
takes the keyboard without activating the app. Other platforms report
true. The fake reports false while OffActiveSpace is set.

